<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>{{ ansible_facts['hostname'] }} | Traffic Monitor unavailable</title>
    <style>
        body {
            background-color: {{ tmsetup_homepage_colors['background'] }};
            color: {{ tmsetup_homepage_colors['body_text'] }};
            margin: 0;
            padding: 20px;
            font-family: {{ tmsetup_homepage_font }}, sans-serif;
            font-size: 18px;
            line-height: 1.5;
        }

        h1 {
            color: {{ tmsetup_homepage_colors['header_text'] }};
        }

        main {
            max-width: 40em;
        }

        a {
            color: {{ tmsetup_homepage_colors['header_text'] }};
        }

        a:hover {
            color: {{ tmsetup_homepage_colors['link_hover_text'] }};
        }

        code {
            overflow-wrap: anywhere;
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>
    <main>
        <h1>Traffic Monitor</h1>
        <p>The Traffic Monitor's control app isn't answering, so the apps can't check your login.</p>
        <p>
            Open Cockpit at <a href="http://{{ ansible_facts['hostname'] }}.local:9090/">http://{{ ansible_facts['hostname'] }}.local:9090/</a>
            (or the device's IP address with port 9090), log in with your Raspberry Pi user account,
            and start <code>tm-control.service</code>.
        </p>
        <p>Or over SSH, run <code>sudo systemctl restart tm-control.service</code>.</p>
    </main>
</body>
</html>
